Step 1: Create Web API Project
         1. Open Visual Studio 2026.
         2. Click Create a new project.
         3. Select ASP.NET Core Web API.
         4. Click Next.
Step 2: Configure Project
         •     Project Name: StudentAPI
         •     Framework: .NET 10 or any latest version available on your machine
         •     Click Create.
Step 3: Create Student Model
         1. Right-click the project.
         2. Select Add → New Folder.
         3. Name the folder Models.
         4. Inside the Models folder, select Add → New Item → Class.
         5. Name the file Student.cs.
Write the following code:
namespace StudentAPI.Models
{
     public class Student
     {
             public int Id { get; set; }
             public string Name { get; set; }
          public string Course { get; set; }
          public int Age { get; set; }
     }
}
Step 4: Create API Controller
(If the controller is not already present, follow these steps.)
         1. Right-click the project.
         2. Select Add → New Folder.
         3. Name the folder Controllers.
         4. Inside the Controllers folder, select Add → Controller.
         5. Choose API Controller - Empty.
         6. Name the file StudentController.cs.
Step 5: Write API Code in the Above File
Write the following code in StudentController.cs:
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;
using StudentAPI.Models;
namespace StudentAPI.Controllers
{
     [ApiController]
     [Route("api/[controller]")]
     public class StudentController : ControllerBase
     {
         [HttpGet]
         public List<Student> GetStudents()
         {
             return new List<Student>()
             {
                  new Student
                  {
                       Id = 1,
                       Name = "Rahul",
                       Course = "BSc IT",
                       Age = 20
                  },
                  new Student
                  {
                       Id = 2,
                       Name = "Sneha",
                       Course = "BCA",
                       Age = 21
                  }
             };
         }
     }
}
Step 6: Run Application
Run the StudentAPI project.
The terminal or output window will display a local address similar to:
Now listening on: https://localhost:7270
The port number may differ on your computer.
Step 7: Test API
Open the browser and enter:
https://localhost:7258/api/student
